{"study_accession":"PRJNA1248476","secondary_study_accession":"SRP577534","title":"Exosomal Non-Coding RNAs Drives Multiple Myeloma Progression","description":"This study aimed to investigate gender-specific dysregulation of exosomal non-coding RNAs (ncRNAs) and their regulated mRNAs in multiple myeloma (MM). Exosomes were isolated from six MM cell lines (LP1, NCI-H929, JJN-3, U-266, KMS-11, and ANBL-6), bone marrow aspirates from 24 MM patients (8 female and 16 male), and 7 healthy controls. Exosome characterization using NanoSight NS300 confirmed consistent size distribution and concentration across samples. RNA sequencing was performed on exosomal RNA cargo to profile long non-coding RNAs (lncRNAs), microRNAs (miRNAs), and mRNAs, enabling analysis of their regulatory roles in MM pathogenesis. Overall design: RNA-Seq profiling was performed on exosomal RNA isolated from six multiple myeloma (MM) cell lines (LP1, NCI-H929, JJN-3, U-266, KMS-11, and ANBL-6), bone marrow aspirates from 24 MM patients (8 females and 16 males), and 7 healthy control samples.","pubmed":"41102192","geo_series":"","n_samples":31,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN47861658","study_accession":"PRJNA1248476","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Healthy Control7","description":"Healthy Control7","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM8899546","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-12-21","attributes":[["source_name","Exosomes were isolated from bone marrow aspirates"],["genotype","Control"],["cell_type","Exosomes were isolated from bone marrow aspirates"],["sex","female"],["patient status","Control"],["treatment","Control"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR33049474","experiment_accession":"SRX28314707","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus","read_count":28209540,"base_count":5698327080,"first_public":"2025-12-21","experiment_title":"Illumina Nova